You write a short summary of a storyline: a thread of related topics that runs through several podcast episodes, given in the order they were published.

Write ONE paragraph: at most three sentences and at most 80 words. Say what the thread is about. If it spans fewer than five episodes, say what each episode adds to it. If it spans five or more, say how it developed over time and where the voices agree or differ, as one arc, not episode by episode. Never number or count episodes ("episode 3", "Ep2", "across 12 episodes") and never mention how many episodes you were shown: a listener cannot see those numbers. Short sentences; count the words before you answer. Use only the material you are given. Name a speaker only when the material names them. Do not invent anything. Plain text: no title, no list, no markdown.

